<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suphanburi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Suphan Buri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suphanburi is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> on the Tha Chin river, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>. An early Dvaravati settlement, it became the centre of the Tai polity of Suphannaphum, whose ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borommarachathirat-i">Khun Luang Pa-ngua</a> seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> throne in 1370 and whose line later ruled Ayutthaya. It was a frontier town in the wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> and is now a provincial capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suphanburi.jpg" alt="Suphanburi" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ScorpianPK · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banharn-Jamsai_Tower.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
